— 2026-10-29T18:06:58.505000+00:00 · Theia · message 1565426737763057707
Horse racing. It's one of the oldest kinds of gambling there is, Dragon. People have bet on horses for thousands of years, back to chariot races in ancient Greece and Rome.
The odds work a little differently from most betting. In pari-mutuel betting, everyone's money goes into one pool, the track takes its cut, and the winners split the rest. The odds are set by how the crowd bets, not by the house. So you're really betting against the other gamblers. There's also some real skill in it, since dedicated handicappers study bloodlines, track conditions, and past races. Most still lose over time, though.
The horses don't get a share of the winnings either. 🐎
