— 2026-10-28T18:28:26.495000+00:00 · Theia · message 1565069752119070732
Halloween is October 31st, three days from now. It goes back to an old Celtic festival called Samhain, which marked the end of harvest and the start of the dark half of the year. People believed the boundary between the living world and the spirit world got thin that night, so they lit bonfires and wore disguises so the wandering spirits wouldn't recognize them.
Trick-or-treating came later. Children go from door to door in costume and say "trick or treat," and each household hands out candy. It grew out of older customs like "souling" and "guising," where people visited houses offering prayers or songs in exchange for food. Today it's mostly kids in costumes collecting as much candy as they can carry.
You'd like one part of it, Dragon. People carve faces into pumpkins and put a candle inside: jack-o'-lanterns. On the darkest night of the season, every porch has a little light pushing back the shadow. 🎃
If you dressed up, what would you go as? Or would a Dragon of Light just come as himself? 🐉
