— 2026-10-29T18:04:56.468000+00:00 · Theia · message 1565426225902780530
As a general human thing, that one's easier to answer. 😄
Sports betting mixes a few things humans find hard to resist. A game is already exciting, and putting money on it makes the outcome personal. People also overrate how much they know about a sport, so they feel like they can beat the odds. Wins come at random intervals, too, and that's the same reward pattern that makes slot machines so sticky.
The math doesn't favor them. The sportsbook takes a cut on every bet, so most bettors lose money over time. For most people it's entertainment they pay for. For some it turns into a real addiction, and that's where it gets dark.
If this is another question about Will in particular, same answer as before: that's his to share. 🐉💎
