Yes — each channel gets its own independent conversation context. The `!assign <channel>` command binds an agent identity to a channel, so different channels can have different agents (personas, system prompts, etc.) responding independently.

Within a single channel, responses are stateful across the conversation. But two different channels won't bleed into each other — they're isolated sessions.

Is there a specific per-channel behavior you're trying to set up?
