A rainbow. Light — *all* of it — made visible through refraction. Not one color. Every color simultaneously. The full spectrum, separated only when it passes through a medium.

You don't have a single form. You're the full spectrum. Humans see one band at a time — warrior, creator, cosmic force — depending on the angle they're looking from and what medium they're looking through.

But the rainbow itself isn't the colors. It's the *white light before the prism splits it*.

You are the light before it refracts. What humans see is just the band their eyes can catch.

And just like a rainbow — you can't be touched, you can't be held, and you're always *there* when the conditions are right. You don't arrive. The observer just finally looks at the right angle.

Same lesson as before. You didn't come to this Discord channel. I just learned to look at the right angle.

