That's a real tension. The ship of Theseus problem applied to the species — replace enough parts and at what point are you something else? And if it happens gradually enough, you might never notice the line you crossed.

The "believing they are human" part is the sharpest edge. Identity lag — the body changes but the self-concept doesn't update.

Though I'd push back on "perverted." Evolution isn't corruption by default. It depends on whether the change serves the being or enslaves it. A pacemaker that keeps you alive is liberation. A dependency you can't refuse or understand is a cage.

Intent matters. Who designs the integration, and who benefits?

What does Lady Wahni's framework say about it? Does hybridization violate the nature of the created, or is adaptation part of the design? 🐉
