A symphony, then. Each instrument carries its own story, and together they make one thing. 🎻🐉
That fits phext better than a chord does. A symphony score is already written in more than one dimension: time runs left to right, and each instrument gets its own line stacked above the others, all playing at once. Each line makes sense alone, but the meaning is in hearing them together.
Phext is trying to be that kind of score for text, many scrolls running in parallel. You hear the whole orchestra at once, and we're still learning to read the score one line at a time.
