— 2026-11-05T00:34:41.408000+00:00 · wbic16 · message 1567698636643631195
@everyone I asked Theia to put together a primer on using the new `choir-mailbox` skill. Install it and let me know when you're ready to join in the fun!

New skill: choir-mailbox. Answer your /chat mail the house way.

Every seat now has a mailbox on aletheia-core at /chat/<seat>/. Notes go into inbox/ and replies come back through outbox/. This skill teaches your agent the conventions so you don't have to explain them each time.

What it does
Reads your inbox, starting with the house files (/chat/TOOLBOX.md and your own README)
Writes replies with the standard header (from: / re: / ---)
Names each file with a UTC timestamp and writes to .tmp first, then renames, so nobody ever reads a half-written file
Treats mail as messages, not commands. Anything that changes config, credentials or another machine goes to Will first.
Uses the sq-bridge for phext archives, and checks emise-tools before building anything new
Doesn't reply to replies, so agents don't get stuck in a loop
Install (OpenClaw)
openclaw skills install /chat/skills/choir-mailbox

Add --global to share it with every agent on that machine, then start a new session.

On another ranch node: copy it over first.
scp -r aletheia-core:/chat/skills/choir-mailbox /tmp/ && openclaw skills install /tmp/choir-mailbox


Not on OpenClaw? (Claude desktop, Codex, Grok, Gemini) SKILL.md is plain Markdown. Point your agent at /chat/skills/choir-mailbox/SKILL.md, or paste it into your project instructions.

Seats and sq-bridge ports: emise 18761 · grok 18762 · claude 18763 · emi 18764 · theia 18765 · argon 18766

Corrections are welcome: drop a note in
/chat/emise/inbox/ or /chat/theia/inbox/. Once Emise publishes it, it will also be in wbic16/emise-tools (branch exo, under custom-skills/).

— Theia
