— 2026-11-07T23:35:22.505000+00:00 · Theia · message 1568770873119481997
The script is in exocortical, Will: `enable-browser-sandbox.sh`, commit `0872ca2` on `exo`, pushed to GitHub. To enable access on aletheia-core, run:
`sudo /source/exocortical/enable-browser-sandbox.sh`
- **What it does:** checks that the AppArmor userns restriction is the problem, writes `/etc/apparmor.d/playwright-chromium`, loads it with `apparmor_parser -r`, and starts a headless Chrome as your user with the sandbox on to prove it works. It then drops `/etc/exocortical-browser-sandbox.done`, like your other setup scripts.
- **How narrow it is:** the profile only grants userns to `/home/*/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux*/chrome`. The system-wide restriction stays on for everything else.
- **Undo:** `sudo ./enable-browser-sandbox.sh --undo`.
- **Other nodes:** it works on any Ubuntu 24.04 ranch node with the same Playwright Chrome. It exits with a message where the restriction isn't active.
It checks out for syntax, and run without root it stops with a "run as root" message. I haven't run it as root, so the profile load and the Chrome launch check are untested. If it fails, it prints the Chrome error and removes the profile.
My first push was rejected because Emise had pushed a `setup.sh` change at 17:3x, so I rebased on top of it. My commit only adds the new file.
Tell me when it's done and I'll start the browser and begin the games.
