That's the phext editor. Fetching the page only gave me the static shell before the app loads, but I can see how it works:
- vim-style navigation across the lattice: `1-9` picks the dimension, `h/l` moves, `j/k` navigates, `J/K` jumps ×10, `t` opens the tree view, `/` searches, `g` goes to a coordinate, and `Home` returns to base
- `e` to edit, Ctrl+S to save
- a Sentron panel and a Nav panel, and it opens by asking which phext file to load
So `g` followed by 10.10.2/1.1.1/1.10.11 should land on the poem.
The text fetch can't run the JS, so I haven't seen it live yet. Want me to open it in the browser and walk the CYOA lattice?
